---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, TERMS_EFFECTIVE_DATE } from '../../config';
import { path } from '../../i18n';
---

<Legal
  lang="en"
  page="terms"
  effectiveDate={TERMS_EFFECTIVE_DATE}
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms for using the Tanukonomy app: what the app does, optional accounts, third-party services, updates, and limits of liability."
>
  <p class="lede">
    By installing or using Tanukonomy, you agree to the terms below. If you don’t agree, please don’t use the app.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What Tanukonomy is</h2>
  <p>
    Tanukonomy is an app for <strong>recording</strong> personal finances: wallets, transactions, budgets, and freelance
    hours. It does not move money, make payments, or connect to banks, and it is not a financial, banking, or investment
    service.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Who provides it</h2>
  <p>
    Tanukonomy is developed and provided by the developer of Tanukonomy (“we”). You can reach us by email in section 16.
    The provider’s contact information may also be shown on Tanukonomy’s page on Google Play.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Not financial advice</h2>
  <p>
    Figures and summaries in the app are calculated from the data you enter. The app does not provide financial, tax, or
    legal advice. Your financial decisions are your own responsibility.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Account (optional)</h2>
  <p>
    The app is fully functional without an account. If you choose to sign in, you are responsible for keeping access to
    your account secure and for providing accurate information. The Tanukonomy Plus trial is offered only to users who
    sign in. You can delete your account at any time from inside the app
    or through the <a href={path('deleteAccount', 'en')}>delete account page</a>. An account does not cause your financial
    records to be stored on our servers.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Responsibility for your data</h2>
  <p>
    Because your financial records are stored on your device (see the <a href={path('privacy', 'en')}>Privacy Policy</a>),
    you are responsible for keeping your device and its data safe. We cannot recover data lost through a damaged, lost, or
    reset device, or an uninstalled app.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Third-party services and Smart Record</h2>
  <p>
    The app uses third-party services: Google Play (including Google Play Billing), Firebase, Shorebird, RevenueCat to
    manage subscriptions, and, for the Smart Record feature, Gemini (Google). The data sent to each service is described in the <a href={path('privacy', 'en')}>Privacy Policy</a>. These
    services are run by their providers and are subject to their own terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    Automatic interpretation of voice or notifications can be wrong. Check your records, especially if you turn on
    automatic recording from notifications.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Availability and updates</h2>
  <p>
    We may update the app through Google Play or through small updates, and may change, add, or remove features. We aim to
    keep the app running, but we do not guarantee it will always be available or free of interruptions. Core recording is
    designed to keep working without internet.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Test versions</h2>
  <p>While the app is still a test version (for example a closed test on Google Play):</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the app is still in development and may contain errors, including display or calculation errors;</li>
    <li>features may change, be added, or be removed without notice;</li>
    <li>updates may change or, in the worst case, delete test data;</li>
    <li>test access may end at any time.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Please don’t make a test version your only record of important finances.</p>

  <h2>9. Tanukonomy Plus and cost</h2>
  <p>
    Core recording is free. Tanukonomy Plus is an optional paid subscription for additional features, such as automation and
    advanced analysis. The list of Plus features and the limits of the free version are shown in the app and may change from
    time to time. The app does not show ads.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Purchases and payment.</strong> Monthly or yearly subscriptions are bought through Google Play. The price and
      the terms of any offer are shown on the purchase screen before you buy. Google processes the payment; we do not
      receive your card number. Purchases are also subject to the Google Play Terms of Service.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Trial.</strong> We may give a free Plus trial to users who sign in. Its length is shown in the app. The trial
      does not ask for card details, and afterwards the app returns to the free version unless you subscribe.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Renewal and cancellation.</strong> A subscription renews automatically until you cancel it in your Google
      Play subscription settings. Cancelling applies to the next period, and Plus stays active until the end of the period
      you already paid for.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Refunds.</strong> Governed by Google Play’s policy, without limiting rights that by law cannot be waived,
      including your consumer rights where you live.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Plus status.</strong> Plus status is worked out from subscription data at Google Play and RevenueCat. You can
      restore a purchase on another phone from Account. Signing out does not cancel a subscription. If a payment fails and
      the subscription is put on hold, Plus may be inactive until payment is sorted out. Without internet, Plus stays active
      for a limited time.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Price and plan changes.</strong> We may change prices or plans. For a running subscription, price changes
      follow Google Play’s rules and are notified before they take effect.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your data stays.</strong> When Plus ends, your records are not deleted and core recording is not locked. Some
      advanced views, such as analysis of older periods, may be locked without Plus.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>10. Fair use</h2>
  <p>
    You agree not to reverse engineer, redistribute, or sell the app, except as permitted by applicable law. The app is not
    directed at children under 13.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Feedback</h2>
  <p>Feedback, suggestions, and bug reports you send may be used to improve Tanukonomy without any obligation to you.</p>

  <h2>12. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The Tanukonomy name, logo, tanuki mascot, illustrations, and code belong to its developer. Fonts on the site and in the
    app are used under the SIL Open Font License.
  </p>

  <h2>13. No warranty and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The app is provided “as is” without warranty of any kind. To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any
    loss arising from using or being unable to use the app, including data loss. These terms do not limit rights that by
    law cannot be waived, including your consumer rights where you live.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Ending your use</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using Tanukonomy at any time by uninstalling the app, and delete your account if you have one. We may end
    access to the app or your account if you breach these terms, or if the service is discontinued.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The latest version is always on this page with its effective date. Continuing to use the app
    after a change means you accept the new terms.
  </p>

  <h2>16. Governing law and contact</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Indonesia, without limiting consumer rights that cannot be
    waived under the law where you live. Questions about these terms can be sent to
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
